#!/usr/bin/env bash
# Repo pre-commit gate. Tracked (unlike .git/hooks), so it travels with a clone:
#   git config core.hooksPath .githooks
#
# WHAT IT GUARDS. Diagnostic switches rot in a specific, expensive way: a switch named in
# AGENTS.md, CLAUDE.md, docs/ or a run script that NO code reads sends a session chasing a control that does
# not exist. That has happened here (SB_SKIP_GHOST was cited in the project instructions for a
# while and was never in the source at all), and a stale generated registry hides the drift.
#
# It runs in well under a second and passes clean today, which is the point — a gate that fails on
# day one is a gate people learn to bypass. If it fires, either the mention is a tombstone (delete
# the NAME, do not annotate it) or the switch was never implemented.
set -eo pipefail
REPO="$(git rev-parse --show-toplevel)"

if ! python3 "$REPO/tools/diag_registry.py" check; then
    cat >&2 <<'MSG'

pre-commit: the diagnostic-switch registry is stale or names a switch no code reads.
  fix:   python3 tools/diag_registry.py write     # regenerate docs/diagnostics.md
  or:    python3 tools/diag_registry.py phantoms  # see which names have no reader
  Deliberate always-loud stderr writes are marked with a LOGGER-EXEMPT comment beside the
  print (inside the scanner's window, not above the enclosing block).
MSG
    exit 1
fi

# The tools' own self-tests. Each one feeds a case whose answer is forced, so the tool has to
# demonstrate it can produce the OTHER answer. They existed and nothing ran them, which is the
# same defect one level up: a broken instrument still reports a clean negative, now with a
# reassuring --selftest in its docstring.
# Paths named in the LIVE docs must exist. The switch registry above catches an env var that no
# code reads; this catches a FILE that no tree contains — the same defect one level over. It is how
# docs/60fps/ came to name nine files that resolved to nothing, including a "DONE" tool whose
# switch and source were both absent, and how tools/oracle/capture.sh spent months looking for its
# Dolphin binary in an uninitialised submodule and silently using a stock build instead.
# A path that is genuinely gone is exempted by marking it (DELETED) on the same line.
if ! python3 "$REPO/tools/docs/doc_paths.py"; then
  cat >&2 <<'EOM'

A live document names a source path that does not exist. A reader follows it, finds nothing,
and cannot tell whether the file moved or was deleted.

  fix:  qualify the path, or locate where the code MOVED — find it by a hook address or a
        symbol it defines, never by guessing at a plausible rename
  or:   if it is genuinely gone and the history is the point, mark it (DELETED) on the same
        line, which exempts it
  see:  python3 tools/docs/doc_paths.py
EOM
  exit 1
fi

if ! python3 "$REPO/tools/selftest_all.py"; then
    cat >&2 <<'MSG'

pre-commit: a diagnostic tool's own self-test failed, so that tool cannot be trusted to show the
  answer it is about to be used for. Run it directly to see which case broke:
    python3 tools/selftest_all.py
    python3 tools/selftest_all.py --list    # what is covered at all
MSG
    exit 1
fi

if ! python3 "$REPO/tools/structure_check.py"; then
    cat >&2 <<'MSG'

pre-commit: the host application structure ratchet failed. Split the named file at its cohesive
  ownership boundary; do not raise the limit to land growth.
MSG
    exit 1
fi
